    technical_zh: 'CLIP 的训练目标非常朴素：给定一批 N 个图文对，模型要预测「哪个文本和哪张图真正配对」。做法是分别用图像编码器和文本编码器把图片、文字转成向量，归一化后用余弦相似度算出一个 N×N 的相似度矩阵；对角线是真正配对（正样本），其余是负样本。损失函数采用对称 InfoNCE：对每行、每列都做交叉熵，让匹配的 Pair 相似度尽可能高、其余尽可能低。训练时批次很大（论文用 32,768），意味着每张图都要在数万个负样本中「找对对象」，从而得到判别力强的表示。推理时完全不微调：把每个候选类别名套进提示模板（如「a photo of a {label}」）编码成文本向量，谁和图像向量最相似就判为哪类。温度参数 τ 是可学习的，控制分布锐度。',
    technical_en: 'CLIP\'s training task is deceptively simple: given a batch of N image-text pairs, predict which text was actually paired with which image. An image encoder and a text encoder produce normalized embeddings, and a cosine-similarity matrix of size N×N is scored with a symmetric InfoNCE loss: the diagonal (true pairs) should have high similarity, the off-diagonal (negatives) should be low. Because the batch is huge (the paper uses 32,768), each image is contrasted against tens of thousands of negatives, forcing a highly discriminative representation. A learnable temperature τ controls how sharp the similarity distribution is. At inference there is no fine-tuning: each class label is wrapped in a prompt template such as "a photo of a {label}", encoded into a text vector, and the class whose embedding is closest to the image embedding wins. Prompt engineering (the wording of the template) noticeably improves accuracy, which is why CLIP ships with an ensemble of prompts.',
    impact_zh: 'CLIP 证明了「网络规模的弱监督」足以训练出可迁移的视觉表示，开启了多模态对齐研究的主流方向。它被广泛用作文生图模型的文本编码器，并催生了 BLIP、ALIGN、Florence 等大量视觉-语言模型。其「零样本」能力也让图像检索、内容审核、机器视觉的提示工程成为可能。局限在于训练数据带有互联网偏见，且对细粒度、抽象或分布外任务仍会失败；零样本表现虽好但远低于有监督微调。后续研究还指出其鲁棒性提升主要来自评测方式变化，而非真正的理解。',
    impact_en: 'CLIP demonstrated that web-scale weak supervision can yield transferable visual representations, launching the dominant line of multimodal alignment research. It became the standard text encoder for text-to-image models and inspired a wave of vision-language models such as ALIGN, BLIP, and Florence. Its zero-shot ability enabled new approaches to image retrieval, content moderation, and vision prompting. Limitations include inherited internet biases, weaker performance on fine-grained or out-of-distribution tasks, and zero-shot accuracy that still trails fully supervised fine-tuning. Later analysis also noted that part of its robustness gain comes from changed evaluation, not genuine understanding.',
