    technical_zh: 'Stable Diffusion 的工作流分三步。先用一个变分自编码器（VAE）把 512×512 的图压缩成 64×64 的潜表示——相当于把数据量缩小约 64 倍，扩散就在这块「小块」上进行，而不是在百万级像素上，因此又快又省。去噪主体是 U-Net：它从纯噪声潜变量出发，在每一步根据文本提示预测「该去掉多少噪声」，反复迭代约 20—50 步后得到干净潜图。文本条件是靠 CLIP 文本编码器把 prompt 变成 77 个 token 的嵌入，再通过交叉注意力「注入」U-Net 的每一层，决定画面内容。打比方：VAE 像压缩/解压软件，U-Net 像逐步擦除噪点的画师，CLIP 像给画师念要求的导演。最后 VAE 解码器把潜图还原成可见图像。',
    technical_en: 'Stable Diffusion runs in three stages. A variational autoencoder (VAE) first compresses a 512x512 image into a 64x64 latent, shrinking the data by roughly 64x so diffusion operates on small patches rather than millions of pixels, which is both fast and cheap. The denoising core is a U-Net that starts from pure noise and, at each step, predicts how much noise to remove, conditioned on the text prompt, repeating about 20–50 steps to produce a clean latent. Text conditioning comes from a CLIP text encoder that turns the prompt into a 77-token embedding, injected into every U-Net layer via cross-attention, steering what appears in the image. An analogy: the VAE is a compressor/decompressor, the U-Net is a painter that erases noise step by step, and CLIP is the director reading the brief. Finally the VAE decoder turns the latent back into pixels.',
    impact_zh: 'Stable Diffusion 把顶级文生图能力带到普通人的电脑上，催生了庞大的开源创作与二次开发生态，深刻改变了插画、设计、影视原型等行业。其局限与争议同样突出：训练所用的 LAION 数据含受版权保护图像，引发 Getty Images 与多位艺术家对 Stability AI 的集体诉讼；模型也易被用于深度伪造与不当内容。围绕训练数据授权与艺术家权益的法规争论至今未决，成为生成式 AI 治理的焦点案例。',
    impact_en: 'Stable Diffusion brought top-tier text-to-image capability to ordinary computers, spawning a vast open-source creation and remix ecosystem and reshaping illustration, design, and film prototyping. Its limits and controversies are equally notable: the LAION training data contained copyrighted images, triggering lawsuits from Getty Images and artists against Stability AI; the model is easily repurposed for deepfakes and harmful content. Debates over training-data licensing and artists\' rights remain unresolved and have become a focal point of generative-AI governance. Its open release also accelerated a wave of community fine-tunes, custom models, and user-facing tools that reshaped creative workflows.',
